<%# The human-facing verification page. Reached from the
    verification_url an operator's request_kyc returned; the unguessable request
    token in the URL is the only credential — no sign-in. Approving mints an
    anonymized claim bound to (this request + its operator + its subject); the
    underlying documents never leave the human. %>
<main>
  <h1>kyc.demo.kiosk.tech</h1>

  <% if @request.nil? %>
    <p role="alert">
      This verification link was not recognised — it may have expired or already
      been used. Ask the assistant to start verification again.
    </p>
  <% elsif !@request.confirmable? %>
    <p>
      This verification is no longer open (it was
      <strong><%= @request.expired? ? "let expire" : @request.status %></strong>).
      You can close this page.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      <strong><%= @request.operator_id %></strong> has asked us to confirm the
      facts below about you. Nothing else is shared with
      <strong><%= @request.operator_id %></strong> — not your name, date of
      birth, or licence number, only the answers below.
    </p>

    <form action="/verify" method="post">
      <input type="hidden" name="request" value="<%= @request.request_id %>">
      <ul class="claims">
        <% @entries.each do |entry| %>
          <li>
            <label>
              <input type="checkbox" class="claim-check">
              <%= entry[:question] %>
            </label>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <button type="submit" name="decision" value="approve" id="approve-btn" disabled>Yes — confirm these</button>
        <button type="submit" name="decision" value="decline">No</button>
      </p>
    </form>

    <%# UI affordance only: the human must actively tick each fact before the
        "Yes" button enables. This is a client-side gate — the broker's POST
        /verify approve path reads only `decision`, so the two-server test
        harness (which POSTs decision=approve directly, no checkbox fields)
        is unaffected. "No" stays enabled at all times. %>
    <script>
      (function () {
        var boxes = Array.prototype.slice.call(
          document.querySelectorAll(".claim-check")
        );
        var approve = document.getElementById("approve-btn");
        if (!approve || boxes.length === 0) { return; }
        function sync() {
          approve.disabled = !boxes.every(function (b) { return b.checked; });
        }
        boxes.forEach(function (b) { b.addEventListener("change", sync); });
        sync();
      })();
    </script>

    <p class="stub">
      <em>Demo stub — nothing is checked here.</em> You just self-assert these
      facts; the boxes start empty and you confirm them yourself. The
      <strong>real</strong> broker verifies you
      <strong>possess a government account</strong> (you log into a national
      eID or a mobile driving licence, mDL, and authorize the broker to read your
      date of birth and licence category), and later that
      <strong>the account is actually yours</strong> — so you cannot answer for
      someone else, or lend your account to vouch for another person's age or
      licence. This stub makes no such check and no liveness claim; it proves
      the protocol, not that you are really over 18.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</main>
